  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186388209 :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186388211 :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186388212 :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 175921863882